enchilada: MSS: read-only modem/SMEM probe behind mss=1 (Wi-Fi bring-up, round 1)

Wi-Fi on this phone needs the modem: wlanmdsp.mbn runs on the MSS DSP, and the WLFW QMI service
only appears once the MPSS is up and talking GLINK/QRTR over SMEM. Before anything is written,
bsd/dev/sweet_mss.c records what ABL leaves behind. With boot-arg mss=1 it prints the GCC MSS
branch CBCRs (cfg_ahb, mfab_axis, axis2, snoc_axi, q6_memnoc_axi) and the 0x52004 vote bits (prng,
gpll0_mss_div); compares the reserved regions of enchilada2.dtb (removed, smem, ipa_fw, wlan_msa
0x8df00000, mpss 0x8e000000, mba 0x96600000, and mainline's rmtfs choice) with the kernel's RAM range
without touching them; reads the SMEM header at 0x86000000 (SBL version word), the $TOC partition
table in its last 4 KiB and the headers of the global and apps<->mpss partitions; and looks up items
137 (socinfo), 421 (MSS crash reason), 428/435 (SMP2P out/in, decoded when present) and 478-480
(GLINK descriptor/FIFOs). One line sums it up: "SWEET MSS: probe: smem v12, items + - ... (137 421
428 435 478 479 480); mss clocks N/5 on; regions clear; N windows".
Nothing is written. Every access goes through mss_rd(), which only allows SMEM and those six GCC
registers, through one 64 KiB VM_PROT_READ window from kernel_map (io_map unmappable, unmapped before
the next): a stray store faults in the kernel instead of reaching the bus, and io_submap is not
used. SMEM partitions of other host pairs (MPU-protected) are never read, and partition walks stay
below each partition's free mark. QDSP6SS, RMB, the TCSR halt registers, AOSS restart and the PDC
sync register are NOT read: RMB/QDSP6SS sit in the MSS power domain, which nothing here can prove is
powered. Without mss (or mss=0) the function returns before any print or mapping.

